# 3. Findings

## 3.1 `TRD2-PQA-P0-001` — Five dangling source identities

3.1.1 severity=`P0`.

3.1.2 defect=`the subject cites TRD-P0-009, TRD-P0-010 and MPSA-20260829-P0-008 through P0-010, none of which exists in the named source manifests`.

3.1.3 cause=`source IDs were authored from remembered topic/severity patterns rather than validated against the frozen source identity sets`.

3.1.4 impact=`a requirement can appear traceable while its claimed authority does not exist; a parser cannot reconstruct the dependency graph`.

3.1.5 safe terminal=`SOURCE-REFERENCE-INVALID`.

3.1.6 acceptance predicate=`successor contains zero dangling source IDs; every source reference resolves to one exact frozen member; two independent referential-integrity checks agree`.

## 3.2 `TRD2-PQA-P0-002` — Requirement-level source coverage is not total

3.2.1 severity=`P0`.

3.2.2 defect=`the subject omits literal mapping for 7 TRD, 7 structural, 17 schedule, 13 security, 6 traceability and 14 BCA2 identities`.

3.2.3 cause=`input roots and topic-level requirements were treated as evidence of member-level coverage`.

3.2.4 impact=`an omitted defect or successor requirement can receive no remediation while TRD2-REQ-064 still claims all inputs are represented`.

3.2.5 safe terminal=`COVERAGE-INCOMPLETE`.

3.2.6 acceptance predicate=`successor publishes a derived forward and inverse crosswalk for every admitted source identity; missing=0; dangling=0; each identity has an explicit disposition and at least one requirement edge`.

## 3.3 `TRD2-PQA-P0-003` — SREQ and MATH contracts are root-only inputs

3.3.1 severity=`P0`.

3.3.2 defect=`SREQ-001–SREQ-042 and MATH-001–MATH-032 have zero member-level edges despite being declared frozen inputs`.

3.3.3 cause=`the documents arrived after initial authoring and were added only as artifact roots`.

3.3.4 impact=`the future Definition may omit exact source locator, D31, graph, denominator, credit, ETC, calendar, mutex, wait, feasible-schedule or Unknown predicates`.

3.3.5 safe terminal=`SUCCESSOR-CONTRACT-UNMAPPED`.

3.3.6 acceptance predicate=`74/74 identities are enumerated without ranges and mapped bidirectionally; semantic conflicts create explicit Findings rather than silent union`.

## 3.4 `TRD2-PQA-P1-001` — Range notation is non-executable

3.4.1 severity=`P1`.

3.4.2 defect=`two source ranges are used inside sourceIds even though Clause1.3.3 says a range is navigation only`.

3.4.3 cause=`compact human notation was mixed with a field intended to demonstrate coverage`.

3.4.4 impact=`a parser cannot determine membership, detect a missing middle identity or attach per-member disposition`.

3.4.5 safe terminal=`RANGE-REFERENCE-INELIGIBLE`.

3.4.6 acceptance predicate=`sourceIds is an explicit duplicate-free array of exact identities; ranges may appear only in non-authoritative narrative`.

## 3.5 `TRD2-PQA-P0-004` — Source universe is under-specified

3.5.1 severity=`P0`.

3.5.2 defect=`the admitted Requirement-universe contract hard-codes a primary-source QA denominator of 2/2, while the Master also depends on D01–D31, amendments, user directives, legal/provider observations, ADRs, registries, migrations, runbooks, routes and the observed implementation state`.

3.5.3 cause=`primary Product specifications and total planning authority/evidence sources were not modeled as separate source classes and denominators`.

3.5.4 impact=`a two-source PASS can omit a binding Decision, a current security boundary or a contradiction in the existing product while claiming a complete executable plan`.

3.5.5 safe terminal=`SOURCE-UNIVERSE-UNKNOWN`.

3.5.6 acceptance predicate=`successor defines finite source classes, selection predicates and separate denominators; every admitted/excluded candidate has exact identity and reason; source-set closure is derived rather than hard-coded`.

## 3.6 `TRD2-PQA-P1-002` — D31 local source was missed

3.6.1 severity=`P1`.

3.6.2 defect=`SREQ-021 and its summary classify the D31 subject/source/value as unknown in that audit, but durable file /Users/tal/Documents/connect/web/docs/postgresql-runtime-role-decision.md exists`.

3.6.3 observed D31 raw SHA-256=`8816a77739a17e94cf9ffcbf5a586db00e001d9d5fdff3bd8e801a0e33e79bb0`; physical identity=`777 lines/54903 bytes`.

3.6.4 claim limit=`file presence and self-described approval do not prove current authority, live provisioning, correctness or acceptance into the source set`.

3.6.5 impact=`inventing D31 remains forbidden, but continuing to report its source as unavailable would create a false blocker and omit an important database least-privilege decision`.

3.6.6 safe terminal=`D31-PRESENT-NOT-YET-ADMITTED`.

3.6.7 acceptance predicate=`successor Source selection evaluates the exact D31 bytes, authority, amendments, conflicts and scope; D31 becomes admitted or explicitly rejected with reason; no unknown source claim remains if bytes are admitted`.

## 3.7 `TRD2-PQA-P1-003` — Product-specific fixes depend on unaccepted extraction

3.7.1 severity=`P1`.

3.7.2 defect=`the subject does not itself enumerate every earlier requested Product fix such as APP_PUBLIC_ORIGIN, dependency-graph Source guard, disabled nonfunctional controls, accessible Dialog behavior, official Meta adapter limits and the Retention/Backup contracts`.

3.7.3 cause=`TRD2 is correctly intended as a Definition contract, but its completeness claim currently depends on a Requirement extraction process that is not yet accepted and has known source gaps`.

3.7.4 impact=`without an exact forward/inverse Requirement universe, a sound meta-schema could still generate an incomplete Master`.

3.7.5 safe terminal=`PROGRAM-MATERIALIZATION-BLOCKED`.

3.7.6 acceptance predicate=`accepted Requirement/Decision universe explicitly maps every binding source statement and user amendment through Requirement→Task→Test→Evidence→Gate before Program materialization`.

# 4. Required successor corrections

4.1 create a new TRD2 Requirement-manifest generation; do not patch or relabel the reviewed subject.

4.2 replace every invalid source identity with the correct existing identity only after semantic verification; never infer by ordinal alone.

4.3 create explicit machine arrays for all admitted TRD, structural, schedule, security, traceability, BCA2, SREQ and MATH identities.

4.4 add a bidirectional source-identity→TRD2-requirement coverage manifest with explicit excluded/conflict dispositions.

4.5 separate primary specifications, user/Decision authority, current official mutable authority, accepted internal design sources, observed implementation sources and historical planning sources.

4.6 evaluate D31’s exact source bytes and authority during Source-freeze generation rather than preserving a stale unknown claim.

4.7 prohibit Requirement extraction and Program Task materialization until the corrected successor, its independent reviews and detached exact-root acceptance pass.

